ine/godot/pulls/109779","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109779","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109779.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109779.patch","merged_at":"2025-09-30T23:39:00Z"},"body":"This PR exposes `Thread::is_main_thread()`, which is already part of Godot's internal API - it's just not exposed to scripts and GDExtension.\r\n\r\nI found this while working on a GDExtension that runs some code via `RenderingServer.call_on_render_thread()`, and it would be useful to know if code is running on the main thread (which if \"Thread model\" is set to \"Safe\" would be the same as the render thread, so we can't necessarily check via `not RenderingServer.is_on_render_thread()`).\r\n\r\nBut, also, this is used all over the place in Godot modules, so I think it would be useful to GDExtensions in other circumstances as well.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109779/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":9,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"h